---
import { PRODUCT_MODELS, PRODUCT_MODEL_INFO, PLAN_LIMITS } from '@golem/shared';
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import { STUDIO_PLUGIN_STORE_LIVE } from '../../lib/studio-plugin';
const free = PLAN_LIMITS.free;
---
<DocsLayout
  title="Apple and Apple MAX — Apple Docs"
  description="Choose Apple for limited free use or Apple MAX with an eligible paid subscription. Model choice is separate from permission to change your Studio place."
  heading="Apple and Apple MAX"
>
  <p>The selector beside the message box chooses a product model, not a planning mode.</p>
  {PRODUCT_MODELS.map(model => <section>
    <h2>{PRODUCT_MODEL_INFO[model].name}</h2>
    {model === 'apple'
      ? <p>Apple is the limited free model. It can answer questions and use building tools when Studio is connected and changes are allowed. It is not a read-only Plan mode. The Free plan includes {free.creditsPerDay} Credits per day, subject to its monthly allowance.</p>
      : <p>Apple MAX is available to eligible paid subscribers and has a larger working budget for involved requests. Choosing it on a free account shows an availability notice and keeps your draft; it does not switch your model or charge you. See <a href="/app/usage">Usage and plan availability</a>.</p>}
  </section>)}
  <h2>Availability</h2>
  <p>Paid checkout is not open in the current preview. Check <a href="/app/usage">Usage and plan availability</a> before expecting access to MAX. Extra purchased Credits do not by themselves grant a paid subscription.</p>
  <h2>What changes in Studio</h2>
  <p>Model access and edit permission are separate. Neither choice bypasses Studio pairing, change approval, quota, or tool safety checks. Without a connected plugin, a chat response is not a change to your place. {!STUDIO_PLUGIN_STORE_LIVE && <>Public plugin installation is currently unavailable. </>}See <a href="/docs/plugin">installation status</a>.</p>
  <h2>How Credits work</h2>
  <p>There is no guaranteed fixed charge per message. Actual usage and the plan limits determine the charge. See <a href="/docs/credits-and-limits">Credits and limits</a>; review the result in Studio before treating a build as complete.</p>
  <h2>Training status</h2>
  <p>Apple and Apple MAX are separate product choices with different access and working limits. They currently share a foundation model. Custom Roblox training is in development; a completed independently trained frontier model is not available.</p>
</DocsLayout>
